\section{Empirical Results}

Figure \ref{fig:allocation} shows the weighted-average asset allocation over time. Pension funds moved into real estate and private equity while decreasing holdings in equities and fixed income. This matters because the portfolio became increasingly exposed to asset classes with more complex liquidity and valuation dynamics.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.86\textwidth]{figure1.png}
\caption{Average Asset Allocation Over Time}
\label{fig:allocation}
\end{figure}

Figure \ref{fig:asset-returns} shows monthly returns grouped by asset class from 2006 to 2024. The series show clear instability around the 2008 financial crisis and the 2020 COVID shock. Private equity has the highest average return over the period, followed by equity, real estate, and fixed income.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.88\textwidth]{figure2.png}
\caption{Monthly Returns by Asset Class, 2006--2024}
\label{fig:asset-returns}
\end{figure}

Figure \ref{fig:garch-vol} shows GARCH-implied conditional volatility. All four assets experienced sharp volatility spikes around 2008 and 2020, supporting the use of a time-varying volatility model. The fixed-income model also shows a persistence anomaly in 2022, where the fit collapses toward near-unconditional levels during the sharp federal rate-hiking cycle.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.88\textwidth]{figure3.png}
\caption{GARCH(1,1) Conditional Volatility by Asset Class}
\label{fig:garch-vol}
\end{figure}

The t-copula estimates show meaningful dependence across asset classes. Equity and private equity maintain a strong positive correlation, approximately $\rho = 0.844$ to $\rho = 0.859$, meaning that private equity tends to move with public equity during major sell-offs. Equity and fixed income begin with a more negative relationship near $\rho \approx -0.3$, but this deteriorates toward values above $-0.1$. This suggests that the 2022 rate-hiking cycle weakened the historical bond-equity hedge and reduced the effectiveness of flight-to-safety diversification.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.88\textwidth]{figure4.png}
\caption{Equity--Private Equity Copula Density, 2017--2024}
\label{fig:copula}
\end{figure}

